			<p>
						<table width="95%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" class="border" border="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td class="headline" align="left"><a name="#677">Guild Rules</a></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="body">
							We are The Ancients! Our leader, Ciervox, has a vision that we become the largest guild on the server. We want the name of The Ancients to echo in all zones. We want to become the guild standard, what every other guild strives to be and what people expect in a guild.<br />
<br />
We are a guild of Honor. Honor is not well-taught in this society, but we know what's right. Do what you know is right and you can't go wrong. I would suggest that The Ancients is a guild loosely built on the idealic rules of chivalry. <br />
<br />
General behavior<br />
<br />
You are the single-most important advertising tool we have. You are the face of the Ancients, you are our representative in the field. As long as you are out there, we expect you to be a credit to us. All of the normal rules of the game apply. No Kill-Stealing, etc. We will hold every member to the standard of adult behavior--the minimum playing age is supposed to be 13, but we will treat you as an adult and expect you to behave as such. If an officer gets a tell about your behavior, we will speak to you privately about it; we shouldn't have to do that more than once. Any officer may, at their discretion, remove anyone from the guild if necessary or summon other officers to Ancientcourt for further action. If you think you've been unfarily removed, you can appeal to the Guildleader (that's Ciervox) and the other officers, but his decision will be final. We'd rather not and we shouldn't have to remove anyone, and we'd regret having to do so.<br />
<br />
Watch your language<br />
<br />
I'm no prude, but remember that there are some younger people playing the game. I wouldn't want to see someone banned from the game because their mom saw a naughty word or three on the screen. General rule: if someone would probably object to the words, don't say them. There are several hundred thousand words in the English language...use some of them, instead.<br />
<br />
Help everyone and anyone, regardless of their guild<br />
<br />
We all travel thru the lands and see many characters. Do what you can to help them. Carry extra food and drink, or summon it, for those who run out...refuse the payment, do it because you care. We have limited playing time, so the time you give to another is all the more precious. Those few minutes you spend helping someone, just for the heck of it, will be impressive upon possible recruits.<br />
<br />
<br />
Begging from the guild <br />
<br />
While there is a begging skill built into the game, the experience comes from begging NPCs. Begging is beneath you. You have every opportunity to make of yourself what you will; you have the power to attain anything in the game--when you are ready to get it. You do not need the latest uberweapon and armor to play...Use what you have, you'll get there. If you are not of a level to, at least, attempt the item by yourself, don't ask the guild to get it for you. We are here to support you: we'll help you get your corpse back, we'll get you a rez, we will help you start out again if you lose everything. But committing the guild to get your desired weapon before you're able to use it is not going to happen. Sorry.<br />
<br />
Auctioning in Guildsay<br />
<br />
Let's just not do that. Open a guildauction channel and those interested can join it. <br />
<br />
<br />
Guild entry requirements<br />
<br />
There are no level, class or race restrictions on joining the guild. The reason being that we NEED new people, fresh ideas, new viewpoints. Consider this: any organism that stops growing dies; biological, political, economic--whatever it is, when growth stops, it collapses. We must keep growing or the guild dies. Level restrictions kill growth. Besides that, we were ALL newbies at one point. What a benefit it would have been if we'd had someone to tell us what to hunt and where. Let us be that someone, and help our members to become the players they're capable of becoming.<br />
<br />
Ollie
